(TIM-30 - LANGUAGE.md:4529-4530 says `end` "belongs to the `exit` family
 of keywords and remains reserved". It is not reserved: `a number called
 end is 7.` compiles and prints 7. See Discrepancy 1 and D1.vox; the
 manual's own examples at LANGUAGE.md:302 (`Set end to 5.`) and 960
 (`a point called end.`) depend on the compiler behaving this way.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox TIM-30.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   7
)
a number called end is 7.
print end.
